    "created_at": "2024-01-09T10:50:20Z",
    "updated_at": "2024-01-09T10:50:20Z",
    "body": "I would suggest we fix this as follows:\r\n\r\n- Make \"activation behavior\" and its legacy counterparts null by default.\r\n- Add \"has activation behavior\" which is an algorithm that returns true when \"activation behavior\" is non-null and can be overridden with a custom implementation.\r\n- Make everything that is conditional upon activation behavior use \"has activation behavior\" as the condition.\r\n- Give \"button\" its own \"has activation behavior\" algorithm that takes form into account. \"input\" might need one too?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
